  "caveats": [
    "Trained on a bounded recent-date sample (docs/project-status.md \u00a7 Phase 3 detail), not the full ~19M-row dataset \u2014 do not generalize these numbers beyond this sample.",
    "is_fraud is a SYNTHETIC dataset-generated label (docs/data-lineage.md \u00a7 5), not a real bank's ground truth.",
    "Class imbalance is severe (see split.positive_counts above) \u2014 small absolute counts of positives in val/test make these metrics high-variance; treat point estimates cautiously, especially at the test-set scale.",
    "Both models perform near chance (ROC-AUC ~0.46-0.50) on this sample. The dataset's own (excluded, diagnostic-only) fraud_score field DOES separate the classes clearly (see diagnostic_fraud_score_separation_by_is_fraud above) \u2014 so a real underlying signal exists in the generator's process, but it is not exposed through the transactional/behavioral columns this phase loaded. Leading hypothesis: the signal lives in device/session/IP data (digital_events -> Device derivation, Phase 5), which this ingestion run deliberately skipped for memory reasons (src/ingestion/README.md). This is reported as a real finding, not tuned away \u2014 see docs/implementation-roadmap.md Phase 4's own anticipated risk."
  ]
